activities.teacherDoes:
The teacher leads the class to build a combined block sequence: checking if a player has a specific item, updating the environment state, and using code to place a redstone block. The teacher models the syntax on the board, demonstrating how conditional logic branches based on player inventory states. Explicit instruction is provided on parameter matching within MakeCode blocks.

Modelled Example:
player.onChat("activate", function () {
    if (player.hasItem("gold_ingot")) {
        blocks.place(REDSTONE_BLOCK, pos(0, -1, 2))
        player.say("Gate power initialized.")
    } else {
        player.say("Access Denied: Missing Key.")
    }
})
